normal break-words print:block standard-markdown"><h2 dir=3D"ltr">Project r=
eview: "TrickyRing" (InterviewBaseProject)</h2>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">What it is</h3>
<p dir=3D"ltr">A small <strong>one-tap 2D mobile arcade game</strong> built=
 in Unity 6 (<code dir=3D"ltr">6000.0.50f1</code>) with the URP 2D renderer=
. A ball orbits a ring. Tapping toggles it between an inner and an outer la=
ne. The player collects stars for +1 score and dies on hitting obstacles. T=
here is a menu with a leaderboard, a name-entry flow, a game-over screen an=
d a share-screenshot button. Product name is <code dir=3D"ltr">TrickyRing</=
code>, Android (IL2CPP, min SDK 23) and iOS targets, orientation set to aut=
o-rotate.</p>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">Flow</h3>
<p dir=3D"ltr">Scenes in build order: <strong>Splash =E2=86=92 Loading =E2=
=86=92 Menu =E2=86=92 Game</strong>.</p>
<ol dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>Splash:</strong> fades in and out, sets the frame rate to 60, t=
hen loads the next scene.</li>
<li><strong>Loading:</strong> fake progress bar. If <code dir=3D"ltr">First=
Login</code> isn't set, <code dir=3D"ltr">NameChecker</code> asks for a pla=
yer name, then loads Menu.</li>
<li><strong>Menu:</strong> three swipeable tabs (Shop, Game, LeaderBoard).<=
/li>
<li><strong>Game:</strong> Start destroys the menu's <code dir=3D"ltr">Even=
tSystem</code> and camera, additively loads Scene_Game, then unloads Scene_=
Menu.</li>
<li><strong>Game over:</strong> shows an animated panel with Restart, Home =
and Share buttons.</li>
</ol>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">Architecture</h3>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>ScriptableObject event channels</strong> (<code dir=3D"ltr">Nul=
lEvent</code>, <code dir=3D"ltr">IntEvent</code>) are the main decoupling m=
echanism. Nearly every script subscribes in <code dir=3D"ltr">OnEnable</cod=
e> and unsubscribes in <code dir=3D"ltr">OnDisable</code>, with the event a=
ssets wired in the inspector.</li>
<li><strong><code dir=3D"ltr">PlayerPrefsSaveService</code></strong> is a S=
criptableObject loaded from <code dir=3D"ltr">Resources</code>. Every save =
also rewrites <code dir=3D"ltr">info.json</code> in <code dir=3D"ltr">persi=
stentDataPath</code> via <code dir=3D"ltr">PlayerDataJsonExporter</code>.</=
li>
<li><strong>DOTween</strong> drives almost all motion: UI transitions, spaw=
n and despawn, the death animation, the tab sliding.</li>
<li><strong>Gameplay</strong> is in three scripts:
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">BallController</code> handles orbit math (angle and r=
adius), tap-to-toggle, and speed ramping from 360 to 1200 =C2=B0/s.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">ObstacleManager</code> does spawning, with a min-dist=
ance check and up to 50 attempts.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">GameSceneAnimationManager</code> handles intro and ou=
tro choreography.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> every star pickup replaces 40% of the obst=
acles. A new obstacle is added every 100 points.</li>
<li><strong>Leaderboard:</strong> 5,105 names from <code dir=3D"ltr">common=
_names.txt</code> get random scores. The user is inserted by binary search,=
 and the list is virtualized with a pool of 20 rows.</li>
<li><strong><code dir=3D"ltr">AudioManager</code></strong> is a <code dir=
=3D"ltr">DontDestroyOnLoad</code> singleton. It handles SFX through <code d=
ir=3D"ltr">PlayOneShot</code> and cross-fades music per scene.</li>
<li><strong>Third-party:</strong> DOTween, NaughtyAttributes, NativeShare, =
TextMeshPro. Packages are URP 17.0.4, Input System 1.14.2, and a few unused=
 defaults.</li>
<li><strong>Code size:</strong> about 2,450 lines across roughly 35 scripts=
, all namespaced and short.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">Bugs and issues I found</h3>
<p dir=3D"ltr"><strong>Likely real bugs</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>High score key mismatch.</strong> <code dir=3D"ltr">HomePanel</=
code> reads <code dir=3D"ltr">"PlayerHighScore"</code>, but the game saves =
to <code dir=3D"ltr">"PlayerScore"</code>. The menu's high score never upda=
tes. <code dir=3D"ltr">PlayerDataJsonExporter</code> reads a third key, <co=
de dir=3D"ltr">"Score"</code> (default 6000), which is never written, so th=
e exported JSON score is always 6000.</li>
<li><strong>Leaderboard ranks are off by one.</strong> In <code dir=3D"ltr"=
>InsertUserCoroutine</code>, <code dir=3D"ltr">players[j].rank =3D j</code>=
 should be <code dir=3D"ltr">j + 1</code>. The loop also starts at index 1,=
 so <code dir=3D"ltr">players[0]</code> keeps a stale random rank from befo=
re sorting. The user's own rank is overwritten too, and that wrong value is=
 what gets saved as <code dir=3D"ltr">PlayerRank</code>.</li>
<li><strong><code dir=3D"ltr">_lastScoreStep</code> is never reset</strong>=
 in <code dir=3D"ltr">ObstacleManager</code> on restart. After a run, the "=
add an obstacle every 100 points" rule won't trigger again until the old st=
ep is exceeded.</li>
<li><strong>High score default of 5000.</strong> With +1 per star, a new pl=
ayer can't realistically set a high score, so it never saves. The leaderboa=
rd and game-over UI also show 5000 as the starting record.</li>
<li><strong>No game-over guard in <code dir=3D"ltr">BallController</code>.<=
/strong> <code dir=3D"ltr">canMove</code> stays true after death, so taps s=
till toggle the radius. <code dir=3D"ltr">OnGameEnded</code> can be raised =
more than once.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"ltr"><strong>Fragility and code quality</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">HomePanel.StartGame</code> destroys the <code dir=3D"=
ltr">EventSystem</code> and camera using <code dir=3D"ltr">FindFirstObjectB=
yType</code> and swaps scenes additively. This works but is brittle.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">GameVisualScaleOnLandscape</code> relies on <code dir=
=3D"ltr">OnRectTransformDimensionsChange</code>, but it sits on a plain <co=
de dir=3D"ltr">Transform</code> (I checked the scene). That callback only f=
ires on RectTransforms, so rotating mid-session won't re-scale.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">BallController</code> uses legacy <code dir=3D"ltr">I=
nput.GetMouseButtonDown</code> even though the new Input System is installe=
d and <code dir=3D"ltr">InputSystem_Actions</code> goes unused. It also ign=
ores taps that land on UI.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">NameChecker</code> subscribes in <code dir=3D"ltr">Aw=
ake</code> but unsubscribes in <code dir=3D"ltr">OnDisable</code>, so it's =
asymmetric. It also does no name validation: no length limit, and whitespac=
e-only names are accepted.</li>
<li>The leaderboard tabs (Daily/Weekly/AllTime) just regenerate random data=
, and ranks are chunk-computed even though <code dir=3D"ltr">loadFrameCount=
 =3D 1</code>.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">TabPanel</code> casts enum values to sequence indices=
. It works only because the sequence is 0, 1, 2.</li>
<li>The JSON export writes synchronously on every save, including each star=
 pickup once the high score is beaten.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">RaiseTest</code> <code dir=3D"ltr">[Button]</code> de=
bug methods ship on the event assets.</li>
<li>Spawn positions have no safe zone around the ball, so unfair obstacle s=
pawns are possible.</li>
<li>Inconsistent UI strings: "Score:" vs "Score :", "HighScore" vs "High Sc=
ore".</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"ltr"><strong>Project hygiene</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li>The Shop panel is an empty placeholder. No script or content.</li>
<li><code dir=3D"ltr">BootStrap.unity</code> is listed (disabled) in build =
settings, but the file isn't in the zip.</li>
<li>Typos in names: <code dir=3D"ltr">AudioManger</code>, <code dir=3D"ltr"=
>Obsticle</code> (also the tag string), <code dir=3D"ltr">PanelSeqence</cod=
e>, <code dir=3D"ltr">LeaaderBoardItem</code>, <code dir=3D"ltr">LeadeerBoa=
rdLoading</code>, <code dir=3D"ltr">Prfab_GameUi</code>.</li>
<li>The bundle ID is still the default <code dir=3D"ltr">com.DefaultCompany=
.2D-URP</code>.</li>
<li>No tests, no asmdefs for game code, no README or git history.</li>
<li>The 3.9 MB <code dir=3D"ltr">Lit2DSceneTemplate.scenetemplate</code> is=
 included but unused.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">Overall</h3>
<p dir=3D"ltr">It's a clean, readable small project. The event-channel arch=
itecture is consistent, and the polish is good for its size: tweened UI, au=
dio fades, a virtualized list, native share. The weak spots are mostly data=
-flow inconsistencies (the three PlayerPrefs keys, the rank off-by-one) and=
 a few missing guards. These are fast fixes. The first two items above are =
the most visible to a user and would be the first things I'd change.</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr">If you tell me what the interview task actually is (fix bugs=
, add a feature, refactor, explain the leaderboard), I can go deeper on tha=
t. I can also write the patches for the issues above.</p></div></div></div>=
