s print:block standard-markdown"><p dir=3D"ltr">I've added the shop, coins,=
 themes and power-ups to the project, but I couldn't open Unity here. Nothi=
ng has been compiled or run, including the unit tests.</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr">Please open it in Unity <code dir=3D"ltr">6000.0.50f1</code>=
 and check the Console. I hand-wrote the <code dir=3D"ltr">.asset</code> an=
d prefab edits, so if sprites or the font look missing, <code dir=3D"ltr">R=
esources/Shop/ShopResources.asset</code> is the first place to look. The pr=
oject is in <code dir=3D"ltr">InterviewBaseProject_Shop.zip</code>, with gi=
t history and five commits on top of the baseline.</p>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">What was added</h3>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>Currency:</strong> a run pays out <code dir=3D"ltr">floor(score=
 =C3=97 coinsPerScorePoint)</code> coins when it ends, and the game-over sc=
reen shows "+N". Every change is saved to <code dir=3D"ltr">persistentDataP=
ath/shop_save.json</code> straight away, with a <code dir=3D"ltr">.bak</cod=
e> copy, so killing the app doesn't lose anything.</li>
<li><strong>Shop tab:</strong> the "Coming Soon" label is gone. The tab is =
now a scrolling list built from a JSON file, using the game's own font, spr=
ites and navy/sky-blue colours.</li>
<li><strong>Failed buy:</strong> the button shakes and flashes red, the bal=
ance pill shakes, and a red toast says how many coins are missing. Nothing =
is deducted.</li>
<li><strong>Themes:</strong> three player themes (ball and particles) and t=
hree world themes (ring), each with one free default and two to buy. Buying=
 only unlocks; a separate <strong>EQUIP</strong> button equips one per type=
.</li>
<li><strong>Power-ups:</strong> three buttons at the bottom of the game scr=
een, usable only while a run is active, with counts that persist.
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong>Shield:</strong> absorbs the next hit.</li>
<li><strong>Double score:</strong> stars count =C3=972 for 10 seconds.</li>
<li><strong>Clear all:</strong> removes every obstacle.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Config:</strong> <code dir=3D"ltr">Assets/Resources/Shop/ShopCo=
nfig.json</code> holds prices, items, section order and the economy. The re=
quirements ask for two power-ups and I shipped three; delete one from the J=
SON to sell only two.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"ltr">For quality, I added a README, a one-page <code dir=3D"ltr">=
Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md</code>, and EditMode tests for the shop rules. There i=
s also a <strong>Tools =E2=96=B8 Shop</strong> menu with "Add 1000 Coins" f=
or testing.</p>
<h3 dir=3D"ltr">Existing files changed</h3>
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li><strong><code dir=3D"ltr">BallController.cs</code></strong> (+6/=E2=88=
=922 lines):
<ul dir=3D"ltr">
<li>Double score needs a <code dir=3D"ltr">ScoreMultiplier</code> property.=
</li>
